    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the test passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) to return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`. Previously four escalation handlers returned plain `application/json` `Map` bodies (`{\"error\": ...}` / `{\"errors\": [...]}`), which failed the new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` (it removes `city` \u2192 400, asserting `application/problem+json` and `$.status == 400`).\n\n**Changes** (all in `src/main/java/.../rest/escalation/`):\n\n- **`ProblemDetails.java`** \u2014 added a `response(...)` helper that wraps a `ProblemDetail` in a `ResponseEntity` with an explicit `MediaType.APPLICATION_PROBLEM_JSON` content type. This matters because OfficeFloor routes the response through Spring MVC's `HttpEntityMethodProcessor`; a preset concrete content type on the `ResponseEntity` is used directly, bypassing content negotiation (the request sends no `Accept` header), guaranteeing `application/problem+json`.\n- **`OwnerFieldsInvalidExceptionHandler`** (400), **`OwnerCityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** (409), **`OwnerIdentityConflictExceptionHandler`** (409), **`OwnerDailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler`** (429) \u2014 converted from `Map` bodies to `ProblemDetail` via the helper. The 400 handler preserves its field list as an `errors` extension member.\n- **`ValidationExceptionHandler`** (400) \u2014 already produced `ProblemDetail`; switched to the helper so it too sets the explicit problem+json content type.\n\nThe existing `ProblemDetails.build` already sets `type` (`about:blank`), `title` (exception simple name), `status`, and `detail`, so every rejection body carries all four required members. HTTP status codes are unchanged. Out-of-scope handlers (403/404/500) were left untouched.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
